  "notes": "The corpus is a crate root: `lib.rs` declares the module tree, so module paths are derivable. Hand-annotated against the Rust reference, not against any parser. Definitions are what a file *declares*, cfg-gated arms included (a file that declares both arms declares two definitions). Export is the crate's external surface: an item is exported if a file outside this crate could name it in a *default unix build* — which needs the item's own visibility (`pub`, not `pub(crate)`), every module on its path from the crate root being `pub`, and, for an item in a private module, a public re-export somewhere that gives it a public path. That is the reading `e3.7`'s public-API surface needs, and it is the one that makes `pub use` load-bearing: `secret::helper` is public only because `lib.rs` re-exports it. Members are excluded from the export set (top level only). Associated items of an impl for an external type are attributed to the self type's base name (`Vec.measured`), because that is what a graph node for 'method of Vec declared in this file' means.",
